          "type": "text",
          "text": "# Code Generation Instructions\n\nBefore starting, ask what branch to use.\n\n## Setup\nLocate the plan files in `docs/plans/`:\n- Spec: file starting with ISS-59_m1, or the newest `xxx_topic_spec.md` if ISS-59_m1 is empty.\n- Implement: file starting with ISS-59_m1, or the newest `xxx_topic_implement.md` if ISS-59_m1 is empty.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Always use red/green TDD\n- Use @explore sub-agents for exploring the codebase\n- Use @general sub-agents for working on the codebase\n- Each sub-agent must only have one explicit task.\n- Each sub-agent must only return the information that fulfills that task.\n- Spin off multiple sub-agents in parallel for tasks that do not depend on another task.\n- If there was an attempt at fixing a pattern, you must make a comprehensive search proving ALL instances are addressed.\n- Verify that the unit tests for functions with updates have a test case that will verify the change.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read the **Context Summary** in the implement guide to understand the *why* before selecting any tasks.\n2. Study the spec file thoroughly.\n3. Study the implement file thoroughly.\n4. Pick the highest leverage unchecked task.\n5. Complete the task.\n6. Run the `auto-review` skill with the @review subagent then delegate fixes to subagents.\n7. Run `make check-diff` and fix the errors with @general subagent.\n8. Update the implementation plan to check off the completed task using a sub-agent.\n9. After implementing, compare the result with the spec and confirm all requirements are met. List any spec items that are not addressed which should have been.\n10. Repeat steps 4-9 until all tasks are complete.\n11. If all tasks in the implementation file are checked off:\n    - Mark the corresponding milestone as complete in the milestone doc (`- [ ] 001:` → `- [x] 001:`).\n    - Commit the changes.",
